Subject: [P23] mf: stop the presentation clock when a terminal source error ends a start

A restarting seek moves the session to STOPPED while the presentation clock
keeps running. When the source then fails with a terminal error, the command
completes without stopping the clock, so a replacement topology attaches its
sinks to a stale running clock: the video sink starts, the SAR (time source)
is not notified, and preroll never completes. Stop the clock and clear
clock_started in that case. Fixes reload after a terminal seek error
(P22 lifecycle terminal-reload); P19b2 passed only because older clock.c
also notified the time-source sink.
Rebased onto GE-Proton11-11 (SE3-P1)

---
diff --git a/dlls/mf/session.c b/dlls/mf/session.c
--- a/dlls/mf/session.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/session.c
@@ -5081,7 +5081,24 @@
                     if (session->command_state == COMMAND_STATE_STARTING_SOURCES
                             || session->command_state == COMMAND_STATE_PREROLLING_SINKS
                             || session->command_state == COMMAND_STATE_STARTING_SINKS)
+                    {
+                        MFCLOCK_STATE clock_state;
+
+                        /* A restarting seek keeps the old clock running while the
+                         * session is already STOPPED. If that start fails, stop the
+                         * clock too, so a replacement topology does not attach its
+                         * sinks to a stale running clock and never finish preroll. */
+                        if (session->state == SESSION_STATE_STOPPED && session->clock_started
+                                && SUCCEEDED(IMFPresentationClock_GetState(session->clock, 0, &clock_state)))
+                        {
+                            if (clock_state == MFCLOCK_STATE_INVALID || clock_state == MFCLOCK_STATE_STOPPED
+                                    || SUCCEEDED(IMFPresentationClock_Stop(session->clock)))
+                                session->clock_started = FALSE;
+                            else
+                                WARN("Failed to stop presentation clock after terminal source error.\n");
+                        }
                         session_command_complete(session);
+                    }
                 }
             }
             LeaveCriticalSection(&session->cs);
